r_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.047212180961770184,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":21.3,"_gate_insider_own":0.44111001,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Accelerant Holdings, together with its subsidiaries, operates a data-driven risk exchange that connects selected specialty insurance underwriters with risk capital partners. It operates through Exchange Services, MGA Operations, and Underwriting segments. The Exchange Services segment consists of risk exchange, its operating platform that incorporates various technology, data ingestion, and agency operations that serve the needs of its members and risk capital partners. Its Risk capital partners write premiums directly through the Risk Exchange pay us a fixed-percentage, volume-based fee for sourcing, managing, and monitoring the business they write. The MGA Operations segment includes the fees earned by members, predominantly for originating and underwriting a portfolio of insurance policies, reduced by the expenses associated with providing services. The Underwriting segment is involved in underwriting insurance policies and assumption of reinsurance policies issued or accepted by consolidated insurance and reinsurance companies. The activities of insurance companies include property and casualty insurance, policy issuance, and reinsurance arrangements. It serves small-to-medium sized commercial clients primarily in the United States, Europe, Canada, Australia, and the United Kingdom. Accelerant Holdings was founded in 2018 and is based in Grand Cayman, Cayman Islands.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jeffrey Lee Radke | Co-Founder, CEO & Director | Age 56 | Compensation: $3.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 862 people. Revenue per employee of $1.1M ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $468K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $50K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Accelerant Holdings is a mid-cap financial services business with a $4.3B market cap on $913M of annual revenue.","The business throws off $404M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 44 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, thin -120.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 9.0% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 44% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 173% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 191% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.9137815927515498},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $25.5M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 33% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Aroa Biosurgery (ASX:ARX) Shares in Focus: Why Is the Ovine Forestomach Scaffolding Drawing Attention?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/au/stocks/healthcare/aroa-biosurgery-asxarx-shares-in-focus-why-is-the-ovine-forestomach-scaffolding-drawing-attention","date":"2026-11-16","timestamp":1794813840.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.527,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Accelerant (NYSE:ARX) Issues Quarterly Earnings Results","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/accelerant-nysearx-issues-quarterly-earnings-results.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794596211.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","legal"]},{"title":"Accelerant Holdings (ARX) Reports Q3 Earnings: What Key Metrics Have to Say","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3028559/accelerant-holdings-arx-reports-q3-earnings-what-key-metrics-have-to-say?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cnfm-3028559","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794490202.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["ear